<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Badis ibn Habus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1073">1073</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Badis ibn Habus was the Zirid king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> from 1038 to 1073. He made Granada a strong <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> taifa, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> in 1038, annexed Málaga in 1057 and built much of the Alcazaba of Granada. His Jewish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">viziers</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-ibn-naghrela">Samuel ibn Naghrela</a> and then Joseph ibn Naghrela ran the government until Joseph was killed in the Granada massacre of 1066.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/badis-ibn-habus.jpg" alt="Badis ibn Habus" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismática Pliego · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirham_badis_20656.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
